            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Among the urban legends and scary stories traded by Absalom's urban explorers, few are as ubiquitous as tales of \"void bugs.\" Exact descriptions vary, and even camera footage is inconsistent, but stories agree on spindly appendages reaching out from impossible spaces, perfectly tessellated pieces missing from machines, and multi-legged shadows flowing like eerie, gangly waves down corridors just out of view. Some Ghost Couriers have made a point of learning more about these creatures, which they've dubbed terminites.</p>\n<p>Terminites have proved hard to study because they live in a nest built in folds of strange space behind the Universe but accessed through the Ghost Levels. Some Ghost Couriers liken terminites to certain eusocial insects; after all, these anomalies infest the walls of reality like ordinary pests in mundane structures. Truthfully, however, a naturalistic description of these creatures undersells them. Terminites are enthralled reflections of their queen: a cryptic overmind permanently ensconced in the nest she's built behind reality in the Ghost Levels. Few explorers have accessed this nest-reality, and none so far have returned, though disjointed recordings or logs of their travels survive. The queen seems omnipresent in the nest; within, her brood take on a nightmarish infinity of specialized forms. Fortunately, the queen seems content to bide her time, at least for now.</p>\n<p>The most commonly encountered terminites are the workers, fragments of the queen's will formed as scouts and salvagers. Terminite workers focus on breaking down physical objects, usually ones with obscure occult resonance, and returning them to the nest for their queen's inscrutable purposes.</p><hr /><h2>Infestations</h2><p>Invasive creatures plague Absalom Station and resist the most dedicated efforts to eliminate them. Whether lurking in the Ghost Levels or stowing away on starships, tenacious infestations are a constant problem in such a large and cosmopolitan station.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Starfinder Absalom Station"
            }
        },
